Scripts to build and deploy msysgit with Chromium patches.

One-time setup:
- Install depot_tools and append it to your PATH.
- Create a ~/.boto file (be sure to use an account that can push to the
  gs://chrome-infra bucket):
  - python.bat gsutil.py config -b
- Clone the repo containing this README (with submodules):
  git clone <repo_url> && git submodule update --init
- Run msys.bat in the root of the checkout to do the initial git compile and
  create shortcuts for starting the msysgit bash shell.

To patch msysgit:
- Start the msysgit shell from your checkout.
- cd /
- Checkout the current chromium branch:
  - git checkout -b chromium-x.x.x origin/chromium-x.x.x
- Apply any new Chromium patches and send for review:
  - git push origin HEAD:refs/for/chromium-x.x.x
- Repeat all of the above for the corresponding chromium-x.x.x-xp branch :(
  # TODO(mmoss): Maybe just merge these branches with some ifdefs
  # (on HAS_WORKING_POPEN?).

To upgrade git:
- Start the msysgit shell from your checkout.
- cd /
- Create a new msysgit branch from the previous chromium branch:
  - git checkout -b chromium-x.x.x origin/chromium-z.z.z
- Rebase the new msysgit branch to the appropriate upstream commit:
  - git rebase refs/tags/Git-x.x.x
- Create a new git submodule branch from the previous chromium branch:
  - cd git/
  - git checkout -b chromium-x.x.x origin/chromium-z.z.z
- Rebase the new git submodule branch to the appropriate upstream commit:
  - git rebase refs/tags/vx.x.x
  - echo 'x.x.x-chromium.0' > version
  - git add version && git commit -m "Upgrade to git version x.x.x"
  - git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/chromium-x.x.x
  - cd ..
- Update the msysgit branch to use the new git submodule chromium branch:
  - git add git
  - git commit -m "Roll git submodule to chromium-x.x.x branch"
  - git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/chromium-x.x.x
- Repeat all of the above for the corresponding msysgit and git submodule
  chromium-x.x.x-xp branches :(

To patch msys-1.0.dll:
- Start an msysgit shell from _outside_ your checkout (e.g. using the "Git
  Bash" shortcut created by the "Git for Windows" installer).
- cd /c/path/to/your/checkout
- git checkout chromium-msys
- git submodule update --init src/msys
- cd src/msys
- Apply and commit changes.
- Generate a patch file, e.g.:
  - git format-patch -1 -o ../rt/patches.chromium/
- cd ../..
- Add the patch file to the msysgit chromium branch (see "To patch git:"
  above).
- Build and commit the new DLL:
  - chromium/build_msys.sh

To build the new msysgit for testing:
- Start the msysgit shell from your checkout.
- cd /
- git fetch && git checkout -f chromium-x.x.x && git submodule update
- cd git && make clean && make && make install

To build and release the new msysgit:
- Start the msysgit shell from your checkout.
- cd /
- git fetch && git checkout -f chromium-x.x.x && git submodule update
- Bump git version and roll git submodule to include the change.
  # TODO(mmoss): Add these steps to deploy.sh?
  - cd git
  - Bump the last digit (the Chromium release #) in 'version', e.g.:
    x.x.x-chromium.0 -> x.x.x-chromium.1
  - git add version && git commit -m "Bump version to chromium.x"
  - git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/chromium-x.x.x
  - cd ..
  - git add git/ && git commit -m "Roll git submodule to chromium.x"
  - git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/chromium-x.x.x
- Run 'chromium/deploy.sh' to create and push the depot_tools package.
- Update GIT_VERSION in depot_tools/bootstrap/win/win_tools.bat to allow
  installing the new git (update just the "DEPOT_TOOLS_GIT_BLEEDING" version
  to canary the change).
- Repeat all of the above for the corresponding chromium-x.x.x-xp branch :(
